+Proposed: make every explanation identify the compared candidate and capture; show all conflicting/unacquired claims with supported citations. Keep selection deterministic and avoid resolving ambiguity by a tag majority, default branch or successful comparison. Preserve unacquired alternatives rather than promising all-candidate downloads. Separate byte equality, archive metadata, package subtree and broader context in explanations/coverage. Components: sources/producer/comparison, evidence records, report facts and Source/Coverage views. Dependencies: P2-01 and P2-03 citation vocabulary; Q4 must add verified assertions alongside original claims, not overwrite them. Risks: matching wrong-version files earning correspondence, conflating unknown absence with removal and presenting known-member counts as entire-archive denominators. Acceptance/validation: conflict permutations keep stable order and the same unresolved association; wrong-source fixtures cannot earn exact/reproduced correspondence; incomplete or ambiguous scope cannot establish one-sided absence. Retain existing S3, network and omission regressions; use real parser proof for changed acquisition/parser behavior, plus report-view parity and held-out source/conflict classes.
+
+**P2-05 — deterministic findings and bounded build explanations (Q3).** **Bounded local implementation complete; explanation quality unmeasured independently.** Named static relationships cover CRLF/LF, strict JSON formatting that preserves parsed property order and a final local sourcemap reference with exact retained cross-side source-text matches. Host code recomputes each relationship; budget failures remain explicit. Unsupported encodings/maps/configurations and misleading generated names get no exemption. Every changed file retains a raw residual finding, including unclassified manifest edits; no new exact/reproduced correspondence or generation claim is assigned. [Raw comparison](packages/core/src/comparison.ts) emits identical/added/removed/modified/unresolved records and one enclosing changed-byte span, not semantic equivalence. It does not operationally produce `generated_candidate` or build records. The reviewed consumer has a generated-candidate branch, but [the actual generated construction](examples/production-phase1/2026-11-01-completion-01/foundation/benign-generated/report.json) yields a generic unexplained difference. The baseline manifest classification could suppress the generic finding for the rest of that file; current rules always retain that raw residual. Current coverage counts raw comparison scope, not proof every behavior was interpreted.
+
+Proposed: measure existing rules first; add bounded deterministic explanations only for admitted, independently testable relationships. Start with exact byte/line-ending or strict-JSON formatting observations and retained sourcemap-reference/source-content matches, each limited to what was mechanically compared. Build-config, sourcemap and package-layout clues alone remain hypotheses. A supported-unreproduced relationship needs independently checked cross-side evidence, exact member/range links, a named explanation rule and stated transform scope; matching sourcemap source text does not prove the emitted program was generated from it. Read configuration as inert data; never evaluate it or fetch paths from sourcemaps. Preserve raw file changes, all unmatched spans/bytes and unclassified manifest edits; no basename, `.min.js`, `dist/`, comment or build-file exemption. Do not claim semantic equality from an enclosing byte span or normalized text. No new operational `reproduced` result is produced in this phase; retained build evidence remains historical and must satisfy existing validators.
+
+Components: comparison/producer and reviewed rules/boundary, coverage records and Findings/Files/Build/Coverage presenters. Dependencies: P2-01 labels and P2-04 source scope; any new parser/normalizer dependency needs its own exact admission, otherwise leave that explanation unsupported. Risks: malicious-looking inert mutations hidden inside generated output, context outside a subtree mislabeled analyzed, a recognized manifest field masking unrelated edits and unsupported transformations reducing recall. Acceptance/validation: paired benign-generated and inert-mutated cases retain every raw residual; mixed manifest events leave residual changes discoverable; unsupported encodings/binaries/configurations remain explicit. Measure explanation precision, explainable-case coverage, false escalation and abstention by class; thresholds below apply. Add focused negative/no-clue and misleading-clue tests; run full serial core/real parser only when isolation/acquisition/lifecycle changes justify it.
+
+**P2-06 — exact-subject cryptographic verifier admission and integration (Q4).** **Authorized isolated evaluation prepared; admission/integration gated.** Exact released verify 4.1.2 plus bundle 5.0.0/core 4.0.1/protobuf-specs 0.5.2 pass 76 isolated development checks on pinned macOS Node, including two real npm artifact/envelope pairs and meaningful adverse fixtures. The 52-package sigstore 5.0.0 alternative is statically hash/notice-reviewed and not selected for runtime evaluation because it adds signing/TUF/cache/proxy/network surfaces. No production dependency/roots/policy was added. Four additional local worker probes pass: a real positive, large malformed certificate rejection, parent deadline termination and cancellation of a busy cryptographic worker, with exact child settlement and denied out-of-scope file/child-process access. These Node permissions/JS-heap observations are not OS memory/network containment. Authenticated root/freshness/rollback, native Linux and production worker/resource/cancellation admission, the full mandatory application fixture/exit matrix and independent consequential review remain requirements. [Provenance collector](packages/core/src/provenance.ts) fetches bounded registry-only material and always returns `not_checked`; no verifier/root/policy is admitted. [S3 adapter-failure fixtures](packages/core/tests/s3.test.mjs) named invalid-signature/publish-only/wrong-subject/unexpected-signer deliberately treat mock JSON as inert bytes: they are not cryptographic negatives. [Executable semantics](packages/contracts/runtime/semantics.py) require matched binding and verified provenance evidence for positive states and prohibit local archives inheriting success; these are necessary conditions, not an operational verifier.
+
+Proposed: complete the candidate review below, then integrate a verification-only path with retained raw envelope/certificate/log/root/verifier observations. Verify envelope type/signature, chain and signed time, log binding/inclusion under the admitted profile and the subject's exact observed archive digest plus package/version identity. Keep registry SRI and registry publish authorization distinct from a build provenance assertion. Attestation links, certificates, predicate contents or model text select neither code, roots nor network destinations. The application checks signed statement subject/predicate semantics even when the library verifies the enclosing signature. No target package installation is part of verification.
+
+Components: provenance/npm/network/producer/engine, configuration fingerprint, verified evidence and strict contracts; shared reader/presenters. Dependencies: P2-VERIFIER/P2-TRUST decisions, pinned dependency closure and rights, operational positive/negative fixtures and reviewed resource/network profile. Risks: self-selected roots, SAN/issuer/OID mismatches, unauthenticated timestamps, duplicate logs, replay to another package/version, downgrade to publish-only and offline trust-root expiry. Acceptance/validation: real retained npm positives for each admitted format/provider, tamper/wrong-subject/wrong-identity cases and fail-closed resource/network tests pass through producer → verifier → persisted report → all readers. No positive release claim until admission; preserve unavailable/unsupported reasons instead of inventing verification.
+
+**P2-07 — versioned expected-identity policy and exits (Q4).** **Concrete draft prepared, not admitted or integrated.** [Proposal `npm-gha-slsa-v1-draft.1`](examples/production-phase2/2026-11-02-local-01/trust-policy-proposal.v1.json) names formats, exact subject/identity/source/builder expectations, generic certificate OIDs, authenticated root bootstrap/update/rollback/freshness, signed-time/log/SCT thresholds, conflict handling, optional/required semantics, exits and isolated-worker limits. Production policy remains unavailable until this version receives owner/trust admission. [Engine](packages/core/src/engine.ts) binds a `trustPolicyRef` string but records verifier/root `none`, emits `indeterminate` for every requested policy and `not_evaluated` otherwise. [S2 policy/exit tests](packages/core/tests/s2.test.mjs) test this honest fallback and 1-before-2 precedence; exit 1 currently has only constructed outcome evidence. [Types/schema](packages/contracts/src/types.ts) and [schema](packages/contracts/schema/contracts.schema.json) already separate cryptographic-only, policy-verified and policy-result states.
+
+Proposed: a trusted caller selects a locally resolved, immutable versioned policy; bind both its identifier and exact canonical content digest, evaluator identity, verifier version, trust-root snapshot and relevant verification-time basis into configuration/evidence. A mutable filename/URL or familiar policy name alone is insufficient. Rules declare npm package/version/artifact expectations, digest algorithm, expected issuer and signer/workflow identity, repository/full commit/subtree/build configuration, builder ID/build type, required attestation kinds and predicate versions, permitted external parameters, evidence/time/root freshness and handling of absent/unsupported/conflicting assertions. Expectations come from reviewed caller policy, never the assertion being checked. Predicate adapters must explicitly map v0.2 versus v1 fields; unknown schemas cannot inherit semantics. Proposed initial slice: public npm GitHub Actions/SLSA v1; GitLab, v0.2 and other bundle/log combinations stay explicit unsupported until separately exercised and accepted.
+
+Components: policy evaluator, trusted option resolution in engine/CLI/TUI/local-web, configuration retention, contract validators and all outcome views. Dependencies: P2-06 and P2-TRUST; P2-COMPAT if current records cannot express auditable decisions without changing old meaning. Risks: signature accepted as policy pass, policy learned from attacker metadata, unrecognized parameters ignored, stale root treated fresh and finding priority converted to violation. Acceptance/validation: actual pass/violation/indeterminate/not-evaluated reports, documented decision reasons/evidence, deterministic repeatability and genuine CLI exits from the evaluator, with equivalent TUI/web states. Update CLI reference, operating guide, foundation and relevant task guides with implementation, not as a claim in this plan.
+
+**P2-08 — shared report compatibility and assembled acceptance (all Qs).** **Local source/diff/compatibility review complete within recorded limits; phase acceptance open.** G0 types/schema/semantics and historical report bytes remain unchanged. New observations bind revised module, adapter, relationship/comparison and loader code. All six outcomes/AI remain independent; no verifier/policy/model activation occurred. Required independent held-out/claim review and the blocked changed-flow browser journey are not replaced by unit/API/PTY passes. Current [semantic validators](packages/contracts/runtime/semantics.py), [G0 fixture tests](packages/contracts/tests/validate_contracts.py), [foundation tests](packages/core/tests/foundation.test.mjs) and [reader readiness tests](integration/part4/tests/readiness.test.mjs) protect identity, independent outcomes, missing evidence, historic reads and AI state. CLI [summary/exits](packages/cli/src/index.ts), TUI [summary](packages/tui/src/investigation-summary.ts) and web [report view](apps/web/src/report-view.ts) project the same facts; the reader intentionally exposes no universal coverage fraction.
+
+Proposed: retain G0 `0.1.0` for changes it honestly represents; put new versioned decision records in supported evidence rather than smuggling incompatible fields into old shapes. If adequate semantics require a schema change, stop that dependent change for an explicit versioned compatibility decision, migration/reader plan and old-report proof; do not weaken old validators or overwrite reports. Bind changed rules/adapter/policy/root bytes to new configuration identities. Components: contracts/core/shared reader and CLI/TUI/web together, fixtures/guides/examples. Dependencies: each changed item; P2-COMPAT before an incompatible representation. Risks: replay recomputing new findings, old consumers coercing unknown states and same report ID hiding different rule identities. Acceptance: old report bytes/digests/IDs/outcomes/findings remain unchanged on reopen; new observations carry new code/config identities; missing evidence stays metadata-only. Same saved report has identical facts in all interfaces; separately acquired runs are compared only under equivalent profiles/options. Use focused actual PTY/browser journeys for changed finding/citation/policy flows, including keyboard/focus/Back, long values and missing content. Preserve the [59 confirmed TUI directions](docs/Design/TUI%20Design%20Contract%20v1.0.0.md); no redesign, design freeze or repetition of accepted Phase 1 tasks is implied.
